Reanimate: If the user is reduced to 0 Wounds while it still has unused attack actions in the round, it sacrifices one attack action and revives 4 Priority ticks after it was knocked out. The user will revive with a number of Wounds equal to the number taken that were not dealt by super-effective attacks, and cannot revive if it was defeated entirely using super-effective attacks. When reviving, the user loses all active power-ups and purges all negative status effects from itself.

Swarm (Drakloak): Upon switching in, the user generates a single Dreepy, which shares all of the user's Merits, its base Dodge (Speed + Evasion) score, and may select its own Abilities. This Dreepy does not act independently; instead, the user may place one additional attacking move that it knows on any action that already has one, which will be performed by Dreepy at the user's Priority regardless of its Speed, expending the user's Energy, and which cannot not form combination moves. Dreepy benefits from any support moves that the user uses, regardless of whether or not it could learn them, and any moves used by Dreepy are treated as if used by the primary if it would be beneficial. This Dreepy is targeted independently, and can be commanded to defend the user of this ability. If the user replaces In-Training with this Ability while evolving into Drakloak, the user will keep its Ace merit, but only apply its bonuses to its Dreepy.

Infiltrator (Drakloak): The user applies a -1 penalty to Aim and Melee and -2 penalty to attack Priority to all opponents attempting to attack it. Opponents whose Aim or Melee are reduced to half their original value or lower when attacking the user cannot attack it at all with moves using that Skill, except those that target all opponents. If the user attacks an opponent that is suffering from Aim / Melee penalties against it, it treats their Dodge and Defense as if they had a -2 maneuver-based penalty that overlaps instead of stacking with the penalties from Aggressive, Counter, No Guard, or sleep. This ability stops functioning for 4 Priority ticks after the user attacks, or is Wounded by an attack.

No Guard (Dragapult): Can convert the mandatory Defensive Reaction into an attack action at -2 Priority, incurring a -2 penalty to Dodge and Defense for the duration of the round. If no Defensive Reaction was used, attacks with same-type attack bonus gain their clash bonuses on normal attacks if any exist, and all attacks within the round benefit from a +2 bonus to Speed and +2 bonus to damage dice. If two attack actions overlap in Priority, their components will occur at their normal Priority instead of one following the other.

